          "html_url": "https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/commit/96bf42536163436671a2f740c3b0da0aee0d70f0"
        }
      ],
      "message": "test: cover external signer command and chain\n\nAdd unit tests asserting that:\n- GetExternalSigner() with an empty command returns the \"needs -signer\"\n  error before any external process is launched.\n- LoadWalletArgs captures -signer and the chain from the wallet's\n  injected ArgsManager. The chain is set to differ from the global\n  Params(), so reading it from globals would fail the test.\n\nIn wallet_signer.py, check the debug log when spending from a wallet\nloaded with a disconnected signer. A missing signer and an empty -signer\ncommand both surface as the same \"External signer not found\" RPC error,\nso the log message is what shows that the configured command reached\nthe loaded wallet's ScriptPubKeyMan.",
      "committer": {
        "name": "woltx",
        "email": "94266259+w0xlt@users.noreply.github.com",
        "date": "2026-11-02T21:14:12Z"
      },
